Panic dump: reuse card state, early write self-test, misc fallback target.

0148 gets the geometry right but the CMD24 write to the userdata tail times
out right after the panic path's FORCED card re-init (CMD timeout, CMD inhibit
stuck); writes into misc with the untouched early state work every boot, so
0149 stops forcing a second init.

  bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
    - panic dump: `sweet_early_card_init(oe.rca != 0 ? 0 : 1)` - reuse the
      already-initialised card (force only when it was never brought up);
      print the CMD13 (SEND_STATUS) R1 status before writing;
    - new `sweet_early_card_status()` (CMD13) helper;
    - new `sweet_early_write_selftest()` (called from arm_init after the 0146
      early misc clear): safe scratch block `misc_first + 0x80`, save original
      512 B, write zeros, read back + verify, print
      `SWEET EARLYMISC: write selftest OK/FAIL ...` (lba/rc/stage on failure),
      then restore the original block.  `sweetearlywtest=0` disables;
    - panic dump fallback: userdata tail remains primary; if it fails (or
      `sweetpanicdumpdev=misc`), write the same SWEETLOG header+ring into misc
      at `misc_first + 8` with area = (misc_nblocks - 8) * 512 bytes
      (32 KiB + header fits in the 1 MiB misc partition), header last;
      each candidate prints `SWEET PANICDUMP: target=userdata|misc base=...
      bytes=...`, failures print stage+lba+rc, and the fallback success line
      says `SWEET PANICDUMP: target=misc wrote ... -> lba 0x...`;
  osfmk/arm/arm_init.c
    - `sweet_early_write_selftest()` call right after `sweet_early_misc_clear()`.

Expected (cpus=4, sweethaltms=2000):
