+/*
+ * 0147/0148/0149: panic-time console-ring dump into eMMC.
+ *
+ * 0149: reuse the card state that already cleared the BCB this boot instead
+ * of forcing a second init (the forced re-init is the prime suspect for the
+ * CMD24 timeouts), print the CMD13 status, keep the userdata tail as the
+ * primary target and fall back to the misc partition (block misc_first + 8,
+ * 1 MiB partition) when the userdata write fails.  `sweetpanicdumpdev=misc`
+ * forces the misc target; `sweetpanicdump=0` disables;
+ * `sweetpanicdumpkb=<N>` (default 32) sets the ring bytes.
+ * Always header last, bounded, failure-tolerant: any failure prints
+ * stage+lba+rc and the reset continues.
+ */
